&lt;p&gt;This international medical virtual conference&amp;nbsp;brings together partners from Columbia University Irving Medical Center and Universidad Nacional Pedro Henr&amp;iacute;quez Ure&amp;ntilde;a for a cross-cultural conversation on mental and respiratory health. UNPHU will explore depression and anxiety, including stigma and cultural perspectives, while CUIMC will highlight asthma and the role of community health workers in connecting education, care, and community resources. This conference will occur in Spanish.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Kersy Yoirys Medina F&amp;eacute;liz&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a psychiatrist and UNPHU faculty member with advanced training in Internal Medicine, Psychiatry, family therapy, and addiction. She currently serves as Manager of the Mental Health Department at the Vinicio Calventi Teaching Hospital and brings extensive experience in clinical care, academic teaching, and mental health leadership. As the UNPHU speaker for this international wellness lecture, she will present on depression and anxiety, with a focus on mental health stigma and cultural perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Adriana Matiz&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a Professor of Pediatrics at Columbia University Irving Medical Center and Medical Director of NewYork Presbyterian Hospital&amp;rsquo;s Center for Community Health Navigation, where she leads system wide patient navigator and community health worker programs. She brings nationally recognized expertise in community based asthma care and innovative care delivery models that address health disparities. As the Columbia speaker for this international wellness lecture, she will present on asthma and the role of community health workers in connecting clinical education with patient centered and community based resources.&lt;/p&gt;

