&lt;p&gt;Marseille, 1815. All of young Edmond Dant&amp;egrave;s&amp;rsquo; dreams are about to come true &amp;ndash;promoted to ship&amp;rsquo;s captain he can finally marry the love of his life, Mercedes. But his success inspires jealousy from various quarters. Betrayed by his rivals and denounced as a member of a pro-Bonaparte conspiracy, he is imprisoned without trial at the Ch&amp;acirc;teau d&amp;rsquo;If, with no hope of return.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After fourteen years of secret instruction by fellow inmate Abb&amp;eacute; Faria, Dant&amp;egrave;s manages to escape and to get hold of the legendary treasure hidden on the isle of Monte Cristo. Now with a huge fortune, he hatches an extraordinary plan to exact the vengeance he craves. Assuming multiple identities &amp;ndash;&amp;ldquo;the Count of Monte Cristo&amp;rdquo; among them &amp;ndash;Dant&amp;egrave;s first courts his enemies, now highly placed dignitaries, the better to strike them down. But the price of revenge is heavy for one&amp;rsquo;s soul.&lt;/p&gt;
